2024-09-05 16:30:20,950 - app - INFO - Analysis result: {'overall_feedback': "Alright, folks, gather 'round, cause we're about to dissect a resume that's about as smooth as a roller coaster built by a toddler.  OLUSEGUN TEW OGBADE, you got some hustle, I'll give you that. You're throwing so many words at the wall, hoping some of it sticks, like a desperate artist trying to paint a masterpiece with a single-use paintbrush.  You're like a buffet of tech buzzwords, but with no main course.  You talk a big game, but I ain't seeing the championship trophies, I'm seeing the participation ribbons.  Just remember, a resume's not about how many words you can cram in, it's about showing your value in a clear, concise, and entertaining way.  So, tighten up that  act,  bud, and let's make this resume something worth reading.", 'feedback_cards': [{'title': 'Summary', 'description': 'Olusesgun, you\'re a walking, talking list of skills and aspirations.  "Impactful solutions," "leading a team," "optimizing systems"... it\'s like you\'re trying to convince us you\'re a superhero,  not a software developer.  My dude,  chill out, take a deep breath, and let your achievements speak for themselves.  You\'re not saving the world, just building websites and apps.  But hey,  maybe you can add \'saving the world from boring resumes\' to your skills.'}, {'title': 'Experience', 'description': "This is the section where Olusesgun's resume  turns into a  'who's who' of African banks.  Dude, you've been working at every financial institution from Accra to Gambia!   You're the LeBron James of  banking apps,  hitting every market with your  tech skills.  But seriously,  we need some specifics here.  Instead of just listing off companies and tasks,  give us some concrete numbers, some hard data.  How much time did you save?  How many bugs did you squash?  How many times did you make your boss say, 'Wow, that's impressive'?  Show us the  results,  not just the  roster."}, {'title': 'Skills', 'description': "Olusesgun's skills section reads like a  'Tech Buzzword Bingo' card.  You got 'Java', 'Python', 'Dart', 'SQL', 'PL/SQL', 'JavaScript'... it's a veritable orchestra of programming languages.  But,  listen up,  we gotta  tone it down a notch.  No one's impressed by a list of tools.  Show us how you use them to solve real-world problems.  Don't just tell us you're fluent in JavaScript,  tell us how you built a killer web app using it.  Remember,  skills are like a toolbox,  it's the craftsmanship that makes the difference."}, {'title': 'Education', 'description': 'Well, at least Olusesgun got a college degree.  No shame in that. But,  you know,  it\'s always good to throw a little humor into the mix.   Something like,  "Graduated with honors… from the school of hard knocks. (Okay, not really. It was Catholic University College, Ghana.  But that\'s a bit less exciting, huh?)"   Just a thought.  You gotta  keep \'em entertained,  Olusesgun.  Remember,  you\'re selling yourself,  so make it a fun show.'}, {'title': 'Contact Information', 'description': 'Alright, folks,  let\'s talk about the contact information.  Olusesgun,  you\'re throwing so many links at me, I feel like I\'m on a  spam campaign.  LinkedIn,  email,  website…  you\'re trying to build a  personal network,  not a  social media empire.  Pick a few key channels and stick with them.  And,  for the love of all things digital,  fix that URL.  "https://www .link edin.com/in/bamidele-te wogbade/"?  What is this,  a  typo-infused maze?  Clean it up,  make it easy for potential employers to find you.  It\'s all about that first impression, and yours is looking a little  shaky right now.'}]}
